  "name": "Question 6",
  "problem": "A rumor is spreading in a school of $2\\,000$ students. The rate of growth in the number of people $P(t)$ who have heard the rumor is jointly proportional to the number of people who have heard the rumor at time $t,$ measured in hours, and the number who have not heard the rumor. If the constant of proportionality is $2.5,$ which differential equation could be used to model $P(t)?$",
